      "category": "security",
      "title": "Validate HTML inside ChoiceFormat branches instead of discarding it",
      "body": "This replacement removes the entire ChoiceFormat expression before checking HTML, including all branch text. For example, a translated linkExpirationFormatter.timePeriodUnit.minutes value of `{0,choice,0#minutes|1#<a href=\"https://evil.example\">minute</a>|1<minutes}` becomes `...` and passes verification. MessageFormat can subsequently expand that branch into an unapproved link in HTML emails. Exclude the ChoiceFormat comparison operator from HTML parsing without exempting the branch contents from validation."
    },
    {
      "file": "js/apps/account-ui/maven-resources/theme/keycloak.v3/account/messages/messages_en.properties",
      "line": 188,
      "severity": "medium",
      "category": "bug",
      "title": "Keep React validation messages in i18next format",
      "body": "This frontend resource uses i18next interpolation with double-braced arguments such as `{{0}}`, not Java MessageFormat syntax. Replacing those arguments with `{0}` and adding `{2,choice,...}` leaves unevaluated formatting text in multivalued-size validation errors instead of the field name and limits. The admin UI resource has the same change. Keep both React resources in frontend-supported interpolation/pluralization syntax; Java ChoiceFormat belongs in the server-side bundles."
    },
    {
      "file": "misc/theme-verifier/src/main/java/org/keycloak/themeverifier/VerifyMessageProperties.java",
      "line": 107,
      "severity": "medium",
      "category": "bug",
      "title": "Prevent overlapping prefix and suffix trimming",
      "body": "The suffix loop can consume characters already counted by the prefix loop. With an English message containing bold markup, a translation `<b><img src=x></b>` sanitizes to `<b></b>`. The common prefix has length 4 and the common suffix length 5, so the diagnostic calls `sanitized.substring(4, 2)` and throws StringIndexOutOfBoundsException. This aborts verification rather than returning the illegal-HTML diagnostic. Bound suffix trimming by the remaining length after the prefix."
    },
